    {
      "block_label": "text",
      "block_content": "O) The argument for forgotten foods feels intuitive. Some analysts say it is in fact inevitable. “Climate change is going to mean almost certainly tastes are going to be forced to change,” says Tim Lang, professor of food policy at City, University of London. We “have to get used to eating other crops” as yields of staple crops fall, he says.",
